  "blueprint_md": "# Automation blueprint: Order intake from distributors\n\n## Process summary\n\n- **Description:** A manufacturer of zoned HVAC controls receives purchase orders from its distributors by email, as PDF or spreadsheet. Customer service keys them into the ERP, checks prices and stock and confirms a delivery date.\n- **Owner:** Customer Service\n- **Executions per month:** 1100\n- **Steps:** 6\n- **Analysis:** <timestamp>, process version 1, rules scoring-v1, LLM ok (fake/fake-deterministic-v1)\n\n## Current state\n\n- **Monthly hours:** 278.30\n- **Monthly cost:** 5,844.30\n\n## Automation opportunities\n\nOrdered by monthly time. Suitability measures whether a step can be automated, not how much it is worth.\n\n| # | Step | Method | Human control | Decided by | Hours/month | Suitability |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---:|---:|\n| 2 | Key order lines into the ERP | AI_CANDIDATE | NONE | RULES | 110.00 | 73 |\n| 3 | Check prices against the distributor agreement | RULE_BASED | NONE | RULES | 55.00 | 95 |\n| 5 | Confirm stock and delivery date | RULE_BASED | NONE | RULES | 55.00 | 95 |\n| 4 | Fix discontinued or wrong product codes | HYBRID | REQUIRED | AI | 22.00 | 1 |\n| 6 | Release orders blocked by the credit limit | HYBRID | REQUIRED | AI | 8.80 | 35 |\n\n- **Key order lines into the ERP:** unstructured digital input without required human judgement\n- **Check prices against the distributor agreement:** clear rules over structured digital input with few exceptions\n- **Confirm stock and delivery date:** clear rules over structured digital input with few exceptions\n- **Fix discontinued or wrong product codes:** Input is mixed and integration readiness is none.\n- **Release orders blocked by the credit limit:** Input is digital structured and integration readiness is partial.\n\n## Proposed architecture\n\n- Workflow engine that runs the steps in order, with retries and an audit log\n- Rules step in the workflow engine with explicit, versioned validation rules\n- Model-based extraction or classification behind a schema-validated contract\n- Automated draft with a person confirming the result\n- Human review queue: flagged items wait for a decision, which is logged\n- Orchestrate the automated steps from a single workflow engine with retries\n- Route low-confidence and flagged items to a human review queue\n\n## Business impact\n\nEvery economic figure below depends on the assumptions listed after it.\n\n- **Hours freed per month:** 134.75\n- **Gross monthly savings:** 2,829.75\n- **Monthly tooling cost:** 50.00\n- **Net monthly savings:** 2,779.75\n- **Implementation cost:** 6,000.00\n- **Payback (months):** 2.16\n- **ROI at 12 months:** 456 %\n\n**Assumptions**\n\n- Implementation cost: 6,000.00\n- Monthly tooling cost: 50.00\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-1>: 50 %\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-2>: 50 %\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-3>: 50 %\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-4>: 50 %\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-5>: 50 %\n- 1 step(s) have no expected reduction and count as zero savings\n\n## Risks\n\n- [RULES / OPERATIONAL] Fix discontinued or wrong product codes depends on human judgement\n- [RULES / DATA] Release orders blocked by the credit limit handles sensitive data\n- [RULES / OPERATIONAL] Release orders blocked by the credit limit is business critical\n- [AI / STEP] Data protection: restrict access and log processing\n- [AI / OPERATIONAL] Exceptions need an owner once the happy path is automated\n\n## Human controls\n\n- **Read the order email and identify the distributor:** REQUIRED. Reviewer decision: Reviewer keeps this step manual\n- **Fix discontinued or wrong product codes:** REQUIRED. requires human judgement\n- **Release orders blocked by the credit limit:** REQUIRED. requires human approval\n\n## Workflow specification\n\n1. Trigger: a new process execution starts\n2. Read the order email and identify the distributor: MANUAL, then wait for a person to approve before continuing\n3. Key order lines into the ERP: AI_CANDIDATE\n4. Check prices against the distributor agreement: RULE_BASED\n5. Fix discontinued or wrong product codes: HYBRID, then wait for a person to approve before continuing\n6. Confirm stock and delivery date: RULE_BASED\n7. Release orders blocked by the credit limit: HYBRID, then wait for a person to approve before continuing\n8. End: record the outcome and the time spent for later comparison\n",
